\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Still with Thee, O my God,
\par I would desire to be;
\par By day, by night, at home, abroad,
\par I would be still with Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. With Thee, when dawn comes in,
\par And calls me back to care;
\par Each day returning, to begin
\par With Thee, my God, in prayer.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. With Thee, when amid the crowd
\par That throngs the busy mart;
\par To hear Thy voice 'mid clamour loud,
\par Speak softly to my heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. With Thee, when day is done,
\par And evening calms the mind;
\par The setting, as the rising sun,
\par With Thee my heart would find.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. With Thee, when darkness brings
\par The signal of repose;
\par Calm in the shadow of Thy wings,
\par Mine eyelids I would close.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. With Thee, in Thee, by faith
\par Abiding I would be;
\par By day, by night, in life, in death,
\par I would be still with Thee.
\par                 Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

